# Context

## Why This Way
The README leads with a screenshot because the demo is the
fastest way to understand what the loop does. The capture is a
real moment: the live server was running, the annealing search
had just recovered the synthetic 340-letter target exactly, and
the result card shows its verified (green) state.

## How to reproduce the screenshot
- python3 zodiac-demo/server.py  (serves on :8408)
- open http://localhost:8408, wait until the candidates table
  fills and the result is verified
- viewport 1512x1150, screenshot the viewport (not full page)

## Gotchas
- networkidle never fires on this page: the SSE stream stays
  open. Wait on DOM state instead.
- The Jev coherence panel shows no judgments unless
  TYPESAFE_API_KEY is set; the shot reflects that (threshold
  line only).
